    "name": "Matriarch",
    "description": "Synthesizers\nAccessories\nSoftware Store\nThe Wave\nSupport\nSynthesizers\nAccessories\nSoftware Store\nThe Wave\nSupport\nFeatured Products\nMessenger\nSYNTHESIZERS\n\nA New Method Of Sonic Experimentation, Communication, And Connection Has Arrived\n\nDISCOVER\n\nLabyrinth\nSYNTHESIZERS\n\nHow Deep Does The Rabbit Hole Go? Meet Labyrinth, An Idea Machine That Aims To Answer That Very Question.\n\nDISCOVER\n\nGet The Latest Moog News\n\nThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google\nPrivacy Policy and Terms of Service apply.\n\nHome\n\n/\n\nSynthesizers\n\n/\n\nMatriarch\nMatriarch\n\nFind a Dealer\n\nAn Immersive Sonic Playground\n\nBased on the vintage circuitry of classic Moog synthesizer modules, Matriarch is a catalyst for creative ideas and a medium for multidimensional expression.\n\nDownloads\n\nIntroduction\n\nOverview\n\nVideo\n\nKey Features\n\nSpecs\n\nResources\n\nWalkthroughs\n\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n\nThe Pinnacle of Moog's Semi-Modular Family of Analog Synthesizers.\n\nMoog Matriarch is a patchable 4-note paraphonic analog synthesizer with a built-in Sequencer,  Arpeggiator, stereo Ladder Filters, and stereo Analog Delay. Create rich evolving chord patterns immediately with “no patching required”, then tap into an abundance of inspiring textures, new sounds, and an endless supply of happy accidents through Matriarch’s 90 modular patch points. Based on the vintage circuitry of classic Moog synthesizer modules, Matriarch is a catalyst for creative ideas and a medium for multidimensional expression\n\nMatriarch: Place / Time / Memory\n\nExploring the Moog Matriarch synthesizer from their personal home studios, multi-instrumentalist Lisa Bella Donna, Ghostly Intl. electronic producer Max Ravitz (Patricia), Anthem / Call of Duty / AssassinsCreed composer Sarah Schachner, and Paris Strother of Grammy-nominated R&B duo We Are KING express four unique sonic perspectives on the new instrument within the context of their own creative environments.\n\nMatriarch: Place / Time / Memory illuminates the interconnectedness between one’s sense of place, our perceptions of sound organized in time, and the impressions they leave behind.\n\nParaphonic Playability\n\nEasily create rich harmonic shapes with up to 4 notes of paraphony that can be sequenced, saved, and shifted with Matriarch’s intuitive 256 step sequencer, or stack the analog VCOs to play on a massive 4 oscillator mono synth.\n\nStereo Analog Delay\n\nWith a deep assortment of synthesis modules based on Bob Moog’s original circuit designs, Matriarch’s 100% analog signal path spans a dynamic sonic vocabulary – from overdriven monophonic bass to gently evolving paraphonic plucks that cycle through waveshapes into a wash of infinite delay trails.\n\nCoupling the power of vintage stereo ladder filters, dual Envelope Generators, stereo Analog Delays, and stereo VCAs, Matriarch delivers a multidimensional sound that empowers the sonic exploration of space and time.\n\n90 Modular  Patch points\n\nThough Matriarch’s semi-modular design requires absolutely no patching, 90 modular patch points are easily accessible throughout the panel via the included 3.5mm patch cables. This powerful electronic instrument is a highly-versatile addition to any stage or studio that can effortlessly transform from a performance keyboard to a fully modular analog synthesizer at a moment’s notice. \n\nIn addition to its standalone function, Matriarch is also an ideal processor of external sound sources and a powerful keyboard front-end for expanding a DFAM, Mother-32, Grandmother, or Eurorack modular system. \n\nMatriarch Features\n\nVOICE MODE\n\nMono, duo, and 4-note paraphonic playability\n\nANALOG DELAY\n\nStereo analog delay w/ up to 700ms of MIDI sync-able stereo or ping/pong style repeats\n\nSEQUENCER\n\n256 step sequencer w/ up to 4 notes per step and 12 stored patterns. Can be decoupled from Matriarch to independently sequence external gear.\n\nARPEGGIATOR\n\nArpeggiator with selectable modes (Order, Forward/Backward, Random).\n\nSEMI-MODULAR DESIGN\n\nSemi-modular analog synthesizer - no patching required.\n\nMODULAR CAPABILITIES\n\n90 modular patch points for endless exploration\n\nKEYBOARD\n\nDiode Wavefolder\n\nSHOW FULL LIST +\n\nMatriarch Specifications\n\nTYPE\n\nSemi-Modular Analog Synthesizer\n\nSOUND ENGINE\n\n100% Analog\n\nNUMBER OF KEYS\n\n49 Full-Size Keys\n\nTYPE OF KEYS\n\nVelocity-sensing with Aftertouch (Velocity and Aftertouch are not hard-wired – available via MIDI, KBD VEL OUT and KB AT OUT jacks)\n\nOTHER CONTROLLERS\n\nPitch Bend, Mod Wheel, Variable Glide, Expression pedal in to CV out, and Sustain Pedal in\n\nPOLYPHONY\n\nMonophonic, 2-Note Paraphonic, and 4-Note Paraphonic\n\nSOUND SOURCES\n\n4x Analog Oscillators with Selectable Waveforms (Oscillators 2, 3, and 4 support Hard Sync), White Noise Generator, External Input jack.\n\nSHOW FULL LIST +\n\nExplore Matriarch\n\nSynthesis is a journey and we hope that these resources help guide your explorations with Matriarch. On this page you will find a growing collection of tutorial videos, patchbooks, tips, and other helpful resources. Each artist's relationship with synthesis is unique and we hope that these guides can help inspire you to discover your own path.\n\nDownload the Matriarch Manual\n\nVideo Walkthroughs\n\nExternal Processing & Controlling Eurorack Modules\n\nIn this video, we explore how to use Matriarch as the heart of a Eurorack system—both controlling and processing Eurorack modules.\n\nWe begin by using the Matriarch’s Keyboard CV and GATE outputs to control the Make Noise Morphagene. Morphagene’s audio output is sent back through the Matriarch, so we can process the Morphagene with the stereo filters and analog delay of Matriarch. By combining Morphagene with the analog oscillators of Matriarch, we create a hybrid digital/analog synthesizer—all controlled via Matriarch’s keyboard. Finally, we use the Sample and Hold section of Matriarch to change the sample played by Morphagene with each new key press.\n\nExternal Processing & Controlling Eurorack Modules\n\nIn this video, we explore how to use Matriarch as the heart of a Eurorack system—both controlling and processing Eurorack modules.\n\nStereo Movement with Attenuators & Inversion\n\nIn this video, we explore just one of the many possibilities that Matriarch’s three attenuators have to offer.\n\nRing Modulation with Attenuators\n\nWhile Matriarch may not initially seem like it has any ring modulators, its three attenuators can each be used to create ring modulation effects.\n\nPatching Velocity & Aftertouch\n\nIn this video, we walk through how to patch keyboard velocity and aftertouch with Matriarch.\n\nRound Robin Mode\n\nThis video explores the round robin mode available in Matriarch’s Global Settings.\n\nDual Filter Explanation\n\nWhile Matriarch only features a single filter cutoff control, you may be surprised to learn that the instrument actually contains two independently controllable analog filters.\n\nHow to Play the Filter\n\nThis video explores different techniques for using Matriarch’s stereo filter as a dual sine oscillator.\n\nStereo Delay Patch Tips\n\nThis video looks at ways to incorporate creative patching to achieve non-traditional delay effects with Matriarch.\n\nChord Memory Tricks\n\nThis video explores different approaches to using Matriarch to achieve a classic synthesizer function: chord memory. \n\nSynthesizers\n\nDISCOVER\n\nAccessories\n\nDISCOVER\n\nSoftware Store\n\nSHOP SOFTWARE\n\nSupport\nForum\nHelpdesk\nKnowledge base\nDownloads\nAll Product Downloads\nPresets\nUser Manuals\nPatches\nFirmware Updates\nThe Wave\nView all articles\nRSS Feed\nAbout Us\nCareers\nTerms Of Use\nPrivacy\nFind A Dealer\nGet The Latest Moog News\n\nThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google\nPrivacy Policy and Terms of Service apply.",
